# The example captures under examples/ are plain git blobs.
#
# They are demo files first — small, curated, and openable by hand — and
# small is the operative word: the whole set is around 150 KB, with the
# largest file under 60 KB. Git LFS buys nothing at that size and costs
# real failures. A `uv`/`pip` install of the Python client from a git
# URL clones this repo and chokes when `git-lfs` is missing or the LFS
# endpoint is unreachable, and every fresh clone needed `git lfs
# install` plus `git lfs pull` before the Rust suite would pass,
# because several tests read these captures through the real reader.
#
# If a genuinely large capture ever has to be committed, LFS can come
# back scoped to that file.

# Two files whose committed line endings disagreed with what autocrlf
# checks out, so every clean tree showed them modified. `text` pins
# repo-side normalization to LF (checkout still follows autocrlf like
# the rest of the tree); renormalized once when this entry landed.
examples/ev-zonal/dbc/pack.dbc text
apps/gui/src-tauri/Cargo.toml text
